# Git: push after edits

After completing code changes in this repository:

1. Run `git status` and `git diff` to review what changed.
2. Stage only relevant files (never `.env`, credentials, or secrets).
3. Commit with a short message describing why the change was made.
4. Push to `origin` on the current branch (`git push origin HEAD`).
5. If commit fails (e.g. missing author), use inline identity without changing git config:
   `git -c user.name="User" -c user.email="user@local" commit -m "..."`
6. Confirm with `git status` that the branch is up to date with remote.

Skip commit/push only when the user explicitly says not to, or when there are no changes to commit.
